      "main.tex": "% Archimedes starter using the official ACM acmart class.\n% Replace the conference metadata and follow the venue-specific author instructions.\n\\documentclass[sigconf,review,anonymous]{acmart}\n\\title{Untitled Research Paper}\n\\author{Author Name}\n\\affiliation{\\institution{Institution}\\city{City}\\country{Country}}\n\\email{author@example.com}\n\\setcopyright{none}\n\\acmConference[ACRONYM]{Conference Name}{Dates}{Location}\n\\acmYear{2026}\n\\begin{document}\n\\begin{abstract}Summarize the research question, method, and principal findings.\\end{abstract}\n\\maketitle\n\\section{Introduction}\nDescribe the research problem, its motivation, and the main contributions.\nA reference example is provided by \\citet{lamport1994latex}.\n\\section{Related Work}\nDiscuss the most relevant literature and explain the differences.\n\\section{Method}\nPresent the approach with enough detail to reproduce the work.\n\\section{Experiments}\nDescribe the datasets, baselines, evaluation and results.\n\\section{Conclusion}\nSummarize the findings and limitations.\n\\bibliographystyle{ACM-Reference-Format}\n\\bibliography{references}\n\\end{document}\n",
      "references.bib": "@book{lamport1994latex,\n author={Leslie Lamport},\n title={LaTeX: A Document Preparation System},\n edition={2},\n publisher={Addison-Wesley},\n year={1994}\n}\n"
